WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:10.770
Request from Ichigo... when watching the television, sit a safe distance from the television in a well-lit room.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.930
For the finals, you will make four different kinds of sweets.

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.780
The first is a pièce montée candy art sculpture.

00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:15.980
The second is a pièce montée made of chocolate.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:18.960
The third is an entremet that does not use chocolate.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:21.500
And the fourth are three varieties of petits gâteaux.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.760
Specifically, a petit gâteau using a glass,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:28.300
a petit gâteau using chocolate, and a petit gâteau that uses batter.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.010
Those are the four subjects.

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.250
And the theme is:

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.850
Dream.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.440
OP sequence

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:42.060
Please make a single creation using this theme as a guide.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.390
Dream...

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.440
That's a very vague theme.

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.730
Impressive, Princess Mari.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.140
That's one of the themes you anticipated.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.390
It's very much a Henri-sensei-like theme.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:00.720
Amano-san, I wonder what dream you will weave?

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:10.040
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:10.040
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.430
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:15.430
I'll give you happiness, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:20.900
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, hapinesu made go!

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:20.900
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, Happiness made go!

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.080
chansu no tobira aketa toki kara kibun joujou ↑ ↑

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:26.080
Since I opened the door of chance, my mood lifted.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.040
youkoso suiitsu no oukoku he

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:30.040
Welcome to the Kingdom of Sweets.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:30.960
Bon appétit!

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:38.330
hajimehane, hetappi demo megezu ni hibishoujin<i>!</i>

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:38.330
Though I was terrible at the beginning, I was diligent everyday<i>!</i>

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.970
「makeruna<i>! atashi」</i>

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.970
「I won't lose<i>!</i> I said to myself」

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:41.980
Courage!

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.760
My dream migakeba hikaru takaramono

00:01:43.180 --> 00:01:48.760
My dream when polished is a shining treasure.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.480
fairy chikara kashite<i>!</i>

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:51.480
Fairy, lend me your strength<i>!</i>

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:56.890
shifon, se shibon, juré, bonjuuru, hatsuratsu furuutsu, raburii made go!

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:56.890
Chiffon, C'est si bon, Gelée, Bonjour, Lively fruits, Lovely made go!

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:02.990
nakitaku natte mo egao ni nareru mahou

00:01:56.890 --> 00:02:02.990
Even if you cry, there is magic that can make you smile.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:08.210
「oishii<i>!」 wo tsukurutte omoikkiri tanoshii ne</i>

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:08.210
「Delicious<i>!</i>」 and making it wholeheartedly is fun.

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:14.210
fuwa fuwa funwari amakute toro kechau

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:14.210
Fluffy, fluffy, fluffiness, so sweetly it melts.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:19.550
shiawase wo ageru yo yumeiro no pâtishièeru<i>!!</i>

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:19.550
I'll give happiness to you, the dream-coloured Pâtissière<i>!!</i>

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.100
ichigo furejie & furanbowaazu, hapihapi makaron, fun fun

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:24.100
Strawberry Fraisier & Framboise, happy happy Macaron, fun, fun

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.310
yume ni eeru<i>!</i>

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.310
Get them in our dreams<i>!</i>

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.900
Presented by Wasurenai-subs

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:39.740
Good morning~ Yumeiro Pâtissière is brought to you by Konami and these other sponsors~

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.890
The match is taking place over two days.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:48.890
Today we come up with the idea and how to create the pièces montées,

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:53.700
and tomorrow from 9 AM to 5 PM we'll complete the work.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:00.590
recipe 37

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:00.590
Unwavering Feelings

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.450
The two teams immediately split off to the middle school...

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:10.500
...and high school cooking classrooms, and began making preparations.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:12.710
Finished.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:18.020
A candy sculpture pièce montée of a white swan,

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.220
and a chocolate sculpture pièce montée of a black swan.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.790
The wave is the entremet, and the fish leaping up are the petits gâteaux.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.930
Plus the extra water splashing up is also made of candy.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.440
What do you think?

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:36.430
I see. So you're trying to express us spreading our wings and taking off toward our dream of becoming pâtissiers, yes?

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.320
Rui, you'll handle the chocolate sculpture.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:44.250
I'll enjoy putting that bossy Kashino-kun in his place.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.990
Unless anyone else has a different opinion, I'd like to handle it.

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:53.570
I would have liked to have you handle the candy sculpture, since that's your specialty, Reiji.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:55.710
But would you allow me to handle it this time?

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:56.840
You, Princess Mari?

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.170
Ah, I see.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:05.730
So you want to show Henri-sensei how far you've come, yes?

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.720
Well, if Princess Mari wishes it, who are we to argue?

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.120
Thank you, Reiji.

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.520
Dreams, huh?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:21.070
Our dreams are to become pâtissiers and pâtissières, yes?

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:24.210
How are we supposed to turn that into a single creation?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.530
That's exactly what we're having trouble figuring out!

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.410
What? You don't have to yell about it!

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.780
This theme is just too difficult.

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:38.840
For something like this, why don't we talk more specifically about our dreams than just "pâtissier" and "pâtissière".

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:41.220
That's a good idea!

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:45.550
It is! If you get more specific, you might come up with a concept!

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:49.530
Kashino, tell us more specifically about your dream.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.480
What's with this all of a sudden?

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:54.510
Let me think.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:58.130
First, I'll win this Cake Grand Prix and head to Paris.

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:01.100
Then I'll knock on the doors of all the pâtisseries around Paris,

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:05.070
learn the techniques of the best, and become the greatest pâtissier in the world!

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.470
I see.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.200
Paris, huh?

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.630
I think a concept is starting to form!

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:12.800
Going well, then?

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.170
How about you, Hanabusa?

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:19.640
I think I've said this before, but the blood of my mother's house of Japanese flower arrangement flows within me.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.750
Moreover, for my father who loved roses so,

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:27.650
I aim for the ultimate coordination in the world of sweets with roses.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:30.390
Roses, huh? That's very like you, Satsuki.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.680
Roses...

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:37.230
I think it's coming together!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.540
Andou's dream is to have a shop next to his family's Yumetsuki,

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:44.440
that combines western and Japanese confections!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.300
I have even bigger dreams now.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:50.700
I want to grow that shop, and open up a branch in Paris,

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.500
and let people from all around the world eat my sweets.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:56.000
Wonderful...

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.560
A branch shop in Paris...

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:04.850
Your dream is to make the strawberry tart that your grandmother made, right?

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.520
Not just the strawberry tart...

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:12.190
I want to make a whole bunch of sweets that make people smile, like my grandmother!

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.380
That's it!

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:28.990
Finished!

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.990
What do you think of this?

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:33.150
Wow, wonderful!

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:35.640
The Eiffel Tower is the chocolate pièce montée,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:38.080
and the rose garden is the candy pièce montée.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.770
You're planning for the shop looking things at the base to be the entremet?

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:43.850
Do you even know what entremet means?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.270
No, I don't...

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.350
Idiot! You don't even know that?

00:06:47.350 --> 00:06:49.720
Entremet means a whole cake.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:53.460
Caramel, will you use magic and call out a few cards?

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:55.160
Sure!

00:06:56.370 --> 00:07:00.660
Cardy-caramelly-comeoutty! Entremet!

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.960
I see.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.270
So those are entremets.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.780
You see how turning them into a store would be impossible?

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:09.770
Yeah...

00:07:09.770 --> 00:07:10.610
That's not true.

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:14.830
We can turn them into stores using the decoration.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:18.560
Well, since you're so confident, I guess the entremet is up to you, Andou.

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.160
I will handle the rose garden pièce montée.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:21.870
And I'll do the Eiffel Tower.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:25.270
You have 9 hours to make it, including lunch.

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.050
I think finishing it would be impossible.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.390
Yeah, I'd say that too.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:33.610
The closer you make it to the actual Eiffel Tower, the more time it'll take.

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:35.850
It'll be impossible to do all that detailed delicate work.

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:37.470
Oh... You're right...

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:39.350
Yeah...

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.190
Even giving it 100%, it's impossible, yes.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:44.740
In such a short time, even <i>you</i> couldn't do it, Kashino.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:45.820
Ah, well...

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:47.930
What're you saying, Hanabusa?

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.740
I'm saying it's too bad...

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:51.740
Then why don't I just do it then!?

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:56.620
We're not gonna win against Team Tennouji even if we give it 100%!

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:59.800
So then we gotta give it 200%!

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.710
I'll give it 200% myself too, and create a wonderful entremet!

00:08:03.710 --> 00:08:06.730
Which means that I'll be in charge of the petits gâteaux.

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:09.590
All right! I'll give it 200% to make those petits gâteaux!

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:11.090
<i>You</i> better put in 400%!

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.400
A-Anyway, everyone... Let's do it!

00:08:14.400 --> 00:08:15.550
Yeah!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.760
It'll be necessary to form a mold for these three parts.

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:32.070
And what about the other sections?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:35.010
The iron girders have to be attached one by one.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.870
We're going to make a mold out of silicone rubber.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:39.980
W-Wait, Kashino!

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.780
I think this will work well for the ivy climbing the Eiffel Tower.

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:49.420
All that's left is to work out the size.

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:51.590
Right. Let's go see Kashino.

00:08:53.190 --> 00:08:57.430
Andou, you're not going to put in some Japanese feel to it?

00:08:57.430 --> 00:09:03.390
No. When you think of the Eiffel Tower as the centerpiece, it's true it seems very western.

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:06.600
But I do want to put in some Japanese taste.

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.620
It seems really difficult.

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:10.660
Don't worry.

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:13.000
I think I'll create the surface like this.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.480
But the issue is what's inside.

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:19.690
I'm trying to think of some way to use anko or maccha,

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:22.210
but the texture is extremely important for entremet.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.550
So...

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:31.830
I was thinking of using a walnut crust on the bottom.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.920
And above that is an anko mousse!

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.400
Right. And finally...

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.470
Ooh, how pretty!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.480
All that's left is to practice!

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.670
For the glass and chocolate petits gâteaux,

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:54.780
I was thinking of making ones that my grandma used to make.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:10:02.260
I can tell how much your grandmother loved you by the way she uses strawberries!

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:05.450
Grandma's petits gâteaux were really delicious.

00:10:10.600 --> 00:10:12.150
Delicious!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:18.390
Seeing your smile makes me happy as well, Ichigo.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:20.420
Will you let me see it for a bit?

00:10:20.420 --> 00:10:23.390
I'll show you an even tastier way to eat it.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.730
You squash the strawberries like this and eat them together.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:34.640
If you do this, I think you'll smile even more, Ichigo.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:35.630
Here.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.320
You're right! It's really delicious!

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.830
See? What a nice smile.

00:10:48.810 --> 00:10:51.020
I'm almost drooling thinking of it.

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:52.370
Oh, that's it!

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:54.340
Let me borrow a coloured pencil.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.160
Finished!

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:01.390
What's that?

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:04.400
I came up with it while you were telling me about your grandma.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:10.150
Why don't you make the strawberries on top candy around the rim, and put a strawberry sauce inside of them?

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:11.400
That'll be great!

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:16.820
Even if you don't go and squash the strawberries, just by breaking the candy a bit strawberry sauce will come out!

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:17.940
Yes!

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:19.700
Yeah, that's a great idea!

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:21.830
Thank you, Vanilla!

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:23.570
Yay!

00:11:27.160 --> 00:11:28.870
Tennouji-san?

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:50.430
Oh, Amano-san...

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:52.310
Hello!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:59.480
Shouldn't you two be preparing for tomorrow?

00:11:59.480 --> 00:12:03.910
The two of us are thinking about what to make for the petits gâteaux tomorrow.

00:12:03.910 --> 00:12:05.380
And what about you, Honey-sama?

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.580
Are you sure you should be taking pictures of swans?

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:12.290
Mari is taking pictures of the swans as reference for the pièce montée she's making.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.590
You're in charge of the candy sculpture pièce montée then, Tennouji-san?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.340
Thank goodness...

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:23.320
I'd never think I could win if you were in charge of the petits gâteaux, Tennouji-san.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.390
It's too soon for you to feel relieved.

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:29.640
Everyone on my team has the same level of ability as I do.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:31.490
R-Really?

00:12:31.490 --> 00:12:35.440
I guess I really do have to put in 400% or there's no way I'll win...

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:39.270
Can I sit next to you?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:41.160
Sure...

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:49.450
So, you said before you're making a pièce montée of a swan?

00:12:50.260 --> 00:12:53.000
You can't tell the opposing team that sort of thing!

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.000
That's not the case.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:13:00.840
She told you because she's just that confident.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:06.680
Amano-san... I've wanted to ask you this for a while.

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.180
Yes? What is it?

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:13.600
I know that you came to this academy on
the recommendation of Henri-sensei.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.940
But where do you know him from?

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.980
We just met by a coincidence.

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:23.920
I happened to go into one of the department stores during the Sweets Festa.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:22.860
I-Itadakimasu.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:28.890
One of the cakes reminded me of the sweets my grandmother used to make,

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.120
and when I talked to the pâtissier who made it...

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.380
That was Henri-sensei, wasn't it?

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.010
Yes!

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:38.670
When my grandmother was young, she studied at the main campus of St. Marie in Paris.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:39.970
That's why the flavour was similar.

00:13:39.970 --> 00:13:41.460
Oh, so that was it.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:47.190
Then he made a really delicious new cake of his for me.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:14:01.360
Now that I think about it, I wonder if my late grandmother made it so that I could meet Henri-sensei.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.940
That's a wonderful meeting, yes.

00:14:06.940 --> 00:14:08.030
R-Right...

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.730
For just a second Tennouji-san had a really scary look on her face.

00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:14.080
What's the matter?

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.520
Oh, nothing.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:20.790
Anyway, how do you know Henri-sensei, Tennouji-san?

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:23.170
The same as you, Amano-san.

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.560
A coincidental meeting.

00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:29.290
Or perhaps, we were meant to meet.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:35.690
This was far back, right about when I entered elementary school.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:41.190
My father's hotel chain was opening a new hotel in Paris,

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.460
and it happened during the grand opening party.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:47.040
I was often brought to parties by my father,

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:50.880
and I hated being gawked at by the adults.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:53.780
Everything would lose its colour and shine.

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:07.420
I felt like everything I saw was monotone.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:19.730
When you sigh, your happiness escapes, you know.

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:28.070
The person who spoke to me at that time was Henri-sensei, back when he was in high school.

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:30.980
Oh, Henri-sensei as a high schooler?

00:15:30.980 --> 00:15:32.290
I wish I could have met him!

00:15:32.290 --> 00:15:36.750
Me, too! I bet he was even cooler than the Sweets Princes!

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:40.660
Are you sure you don't want to return to the party, little lady?

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:43.160
I am just taking a short break.

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:44.950
I will return shortly.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:50.210
You even speak to a pâtissier like myself as an adult, don't you?

00:15:54.150 --> 00:15:56.490
Why don't you try and have more fun?

00:15:56.490 --> 00:15:57.670
Don't force yourself.

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.500
I am not forcing myself.

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:02.010
And yet you sighed.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:06.060
Oh yes, will you wait a moment?

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:11.400
Here.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:15.070
Pretend that you were forced into eating this and try it.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:16.820
It'll make you happy.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:32.140
The moment I had a bite, I felt a great happiness come over me.

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.860
It was like the light of the sun shone down,

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:42.800
and changed that monotone world into one of living colour.

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.060
How is it?

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:47.730
Did it make you happy?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.780
Yeah!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.990
I had always liked making sweets,

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.860
but I had never thought they held such power.

00:16:57.860 --> 00:17:01.800
Therefore, I decided to try and make sweets like that.

00:17:01.800 --> 00:17:03.910
I understand how you feel, Tennouji-san.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:10.990
After that, I tried to become a pâtissière like Henri-sensei, and began my studies.

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.920
Then, when I entered this academy...

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.430
Welcome to St. Marie Academy.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:21.380
I am Henri Lucas, the teacher in charge of you starting today.

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:22.470
Umm!

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:24.640
And you are...

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.790
Do you remember?

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:32.260
Six years ago, at a hotel in Paris, you let me eat a honey pie!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:37.780
Oh, you're that girl!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.560
Yes! My name is Tennouji Mari.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:43.900
Ever since that day, I never sighed again.

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:48.980
How happy I was that he remembered.

00:17:48.980 --> 00:17:55.490
I decided to study under him ever since, and create sweets that'll make everyone happy.

00:17:56.060 --> 00:18:02.070
She wants to create sweets that make the people who eat them smile, just like me!

00:18:03.580 --> 00:18:04.920
What is it?

00:18:04.920 --> 00:18:07.620
N-No, it's nothing!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.260
Anyway, it's sure nice that Henri-sensei came back, yes?

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:18.340
It seems like he will be returning to France once the finals of the Grand Prix are finished.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.680
Oh no...

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:25.470
I still have a lot I want to learn from Henri-sensei.

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:29.000
For that purpose I will win the finals and go to Paris.

00:18:29.990 --> 00:18:32.700
Therefore I will not hold back, even though you are younger than me.

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.920
I will fight with my full strength.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:41.030
Oh, there she is.

00:18:41.030 --> 00:18:42.470
P-President Tennouji!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:48.860
Tennouji-san...

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:53.210
I will, too. We will not lose.

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:54.860
We're going to make our dreams come true!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.820
Amano-san, I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:10.040
Ichigo-chan!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.000
That's some determination you got!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:14.250
I was just caught up by Tennouji-san, sorry...

00:19:14.250 --> 00:19:16.750
No, we need to be that determined.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:18.420
Even if it's just baseless confidence, I guess.

00:19:18.420 --> 00:19:20.050
It's not baseless!

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.760
I got a great idea for the batter-based petit gâteau!

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:24.970
Oh, what do you plan to make?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:28.210
I remembered while talking to Tennouji-san.

00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:32.150
The first sweets I ever made that made Ringo-chan smile.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.980
Oh, the one from Piyo Piyo kindergarten?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:34.770
Yeah!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.230
So then you'll make an apple cake for the batter-based petit gâteau?

00:19:38.230 --> 00:19:38.570
Right!

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.740
Wait, not a strawberry tart?

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:44.780
You're always so worked up about your grandma's tart... What's going on?

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:49.360
I don't have nearly the skills to make that strawberry tart yet.

00:19:49.360 --> 00:19:51.790
No matter how hard I try, it's impossible for me as I am now.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:56.290
But you won't beat Team Tennouji making an apple cake like the one we made back then!

00:19:56.540 --> 00:19:58.270
I know that too.

00:19:58.270 --> 00:20:01.940
But if I trust in that apple cake that made Ringo-chan smile...

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.930
That custard cream!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.650
W-What?

00:20:09.650 --> 00:20:11.210
Why are you yelling?

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.980
You shocked me...

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:14.880
I've got another good idea!

00:20:14.880 --> 00:20:15.690
Excuse me!

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.480
Ichigo, what's the matter?

00:20:17.480 --> 00:20:19.780
Wait a sec!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:22.780
What's with her?

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:27.010
That's what I'm trying to tell you.

00:20:27.010 --> 00:20:29.160
Their cakes aren't very good...

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.370
Nakajima-san!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.510
Amano Ichigo?

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:33.940
W-What do you want?

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:38.410
It's about that apple cake you made for Ayu-chan at Piyo Piyo kindergarten...

00:20:38.410 --> 00:20:40.810
You're still bringing that up?

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:42.470
We didn't steal your design, got it?

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:44.300
That was just a coincidence!

00:20:43.030 --> 00:20:44.300
No, not that!

00:20:44.870 --> 00:20:48.720
The apple custard was really delicious back then...

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.140
I'd love it if you could teach me how to make it.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.150
You've got to be kidding me!

00:20:54.150 --> 00:21:00.980
Why should I teach you, who only got to the finals because the Sweets Princes covered for your mediocre skills!

00:21:02.080 --> 00:21:04.230
Be that as it may...

00:21:04.230 --> 00:21:05.400
Please, I'm begging you!

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:08.240
Figure it out yourself.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:15.670
Man, what a jerk!

